## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run in the repository:

```sh
brew bundle
mise trust                             # once per clone: mise reads only trusted mise.toml files
mise install                           # the uv from mise.toml, checked against mise.lock
mise exec -- uv sync                   # Python from .python-version, dev tools from uv.lock
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
gh extension install github/gh-stack   # optional: stacked PRs
```

Homebrew installs mise and the GitHub CLI. mise installs the one uv version that
`pyproject.toml` requires. uv installs Python and every other tool. With mise activated in your
shell (`mise activate`, see the mise docs), plain `uv` is that version. The git hook runs the
checks before each push. `gh stack` is optional: it helps to open and update stacked PRs.

Editor: install pyright (`npm install -g pyright`) for the language server. It reads `.venv`.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check                 # every quality gate: format, lint, types, tests, coverage
uv run {{package}}            # run the program
uv run pytest                 # all tests
uv run pytest -k banner       # tests whose name contains "banner"
uv run ruff format            # format
uv run ruff check --fix       # safe lint fixes
uv run mypy                   # type check
```

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too. A weekly CI job
(`.github/workflows/audit.yml`) looks for known vulnerabilities and outdated packages and runs the
property tests with new random examples.

